### Project Description

This project is an IPL score prediction system built using historical IPL ball-by-ball data and machine learning. The dataset is automatically downloaded from Google Drive and processed to create match-state features such as current score, wickets lost, overs completed, runs scored in the last 30 balls, and wickets lost in the last 30 balls. These features are engineered from raw delivery-level data using cumulative and rolling calculations for each innings.

After preprocessing, the batting team is encoded using one-hot encoding, and a Random Forest Regressor is trained to predict the final innings score. The model learns relationships between the current state of an innings and the eventual total score achieved by the batting team. Model performance is evaluated using Mean Absolute Error (MAE) on a held-out test set.

To make the model interactive, a Tkinter-based graphical user interface is included. Users can enter live match information such as batting team, current score, wickets lost, overs completed, recent runs scored, and recent wickets lost. Based on these inputs, the trained model predicts the projected final score for the innings in real time.

